# Browser floors of hugolify-theme-design-system
# https://github.com/browserslist/browserslist#readme
#
# Hugo exposes every file of assets/_jsconfig to PostCSS as a HUGO_FILE_*
# variable: this one is HUGO_FILE_BROWSERSLIST, and the module's
# postcss.config.cjs points BROWSERSLIST_CONFIG at it.
# Only autoprefixer reads this list: js.Build has no target, so JS is not
# transpiled from it.
#
# BROWSERSLIST_CONFIG takes precedence over a project .browserslistrc, which is
# then ignored. To override, ship assets/_jsconfig/browserslist in the project
# (or in a module imported before this one): the first file found wins, like
# any asset.
#
# Floors = what the CSS needs without a fallback:
#   - native CSS nesting: Chrome 120, Firefox 117, Safari 17.2
#   - relative colors, oklch(from …): Chrome 131, Firefox 133, Safari 18
# Anchor positioning, invoker commands and text-wrap: pretty are progressive.
#
# Coverage, outside Hugo:
#   BROWSERSLIST_CONFIG=<path to this file> npx browserslist --coverage=FR

